                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_99\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit (fix_commit_diff.txt) removes the entire reload/reloadText\nmechanism from CommandParser, Server, and the Command classes, replacing the\nmutable `helpText` field with an immutable `help` field that is combined with\n`t(commandCode)` on every call to getHelpText(). This is a direct fix for a\nbug in the /help text that occurred after a reload: helpText was rebuilt from\nthe AbstractCommand's `name` field, but `name` had already been truncated to\njust the first word (before any arguments) during construction, while the\nhelp text originally built at construction time used the full, untruncated\nname (including arguments, e.g. \"kick <player>\").\n\nIn AbstractCommand's constructor:\n    if (name != null) {\n      helpText = name + Color.WHITE + \" : \" + t(commandCode);  // uses FULL name\n      int splitIndex = name.indexOf(\" \");\n      if (splitIndex != -1) {\n        name = name.substring(0, splitIndex);                  // name now truncated\n      }\n    }\n    this.name = name;  // stores the TRUNCATED name\n\nBut reloadText() (called whenever the server config/translations were\nreloaded) rebuilt helpText using the already-truncated `this.name` field:\n    public void reloadText() {\n      if (name != null) {\n        helpText = name + Color.WHITE + \" : \" + t(commandCode);  // uses TRUNCATED name\n      } ...\n    }\n\nAs a result, after any reload, /help entries for commands with arguments\n(e.g. \"kick <player>\") would lose their argument portion, showing only the\nbare command name. The final fix eliminates this discrepancy entirely by\nstoring the original full name in a separate immutable `help` field and\nalways computing the display text from `help + \" : \" + t(commandCode)`,\nremoving the need for any reload/reloadText mechanism.\n\ncandidate_99 is the commit that FIRST introduced this exact buggy pattern:\nit adds the `reload()` method to CommandParser, `commandParser.reload()` call\nin Server, and the `reloadText()` overrides in AbstractCommand,\nInvalidCommand, OnlinePlayerArgCommand, and PlayerArgCommand \u2014 all using the\nsame name/helpText mismatch that the fix later corrects. Before candidate_99,\nhelpText was a `private final String` set once at construction with no\nreload capability, so the bug could not exist. Later candidates\n(108, 110, 117, 126) only perform cosmetic changes (switching between\nTranslations.getInstance()/t.get() and a static t() helper, replacing\nliteral color codes like \"\u00a7f\" with Color.WHITE constants) while\npreserving the same buggy reloadText() logic introduced in candidate_99.\ncandidate_131 is the fix commit itself, matching fix_commit_diff.txt exactly.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
